SUMMARY:Deadline: National Geographic Society: The Human Thread RFP
DESCRIPTION:Request for proposals from the National Geographic Society's Ce
 nter for Human Histories and Cultures\, funded by Lilly Endowment Inc. It 
 seeks storytelling projects that document and illuminate the origins and c
 ontemporary expressions of global cultures and religions\, and the wider s
 pectrum of human experience\, through strong creative and research-based a
 pproaches.\n\nOrganisation: National Geographic Society (Center for Human 
 Histories and Cultures\, with support from Lilly Endowment Inc.)\nLocation
 : Worldwide\nAward: Level I: up to US$20\,000 (for applicants new to Natio
 nal Geographic funding\, one year to implement). Level II: up to US$100\,0
 00 (for more established applicants\, two years to implement).\nDuration: 
 Up to 1 year (Level I) or 2 years (Level II). Project start dates must be 
 at least six months after the submission deadline.\n\nMore: https://fundin
 g.nationalgeographic.org/s/fundingopportunity/119Hr000000CohcIAC/rfp-the-h
 uman-thread?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://funding.nationalgeographic.org/s/fundingopportunity/119Hr000000
 CohcIAC/rfp-the-human-thread?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide
END:VEVENT
